main.content:
{{also|Grass}}
==English==
[[File:Steppe, Grassland, Rostov-on-Don, Russia.jpg|thumb|right|Grass.]]

===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:gras|tree=1}}
{{inh+|en|enm|gras}}, from {{inh|en|ang|græs}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*gras}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*grasą|t=grass}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*gʰreh₁-|t=to grow}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|gress|t=grass}}, {{cog|frr|gaars}}, {{m|frr|geers}}, {{m|frr|Gērs}}, {{m|frr|gjars}}, {{m|frr|gjas}}, {{m|frr|gäärs|t=grass}}, {{cog|stq|Gäärs|t=grass}}, {{cog|fy|gers|t=grass}}, {{cog|cim|gras}}, {{m|cim|grass|t=grass}}, {{cog|de,lb|Gras|t=grass, weed}}, {{cog|nl|gras|t=grass, turf, pasture}}, {{cog|mhn,wym|gros|t=grass}}, {{cog|vls|ges|t=grass}}, {{cog|yi|גראָז|t=grass}}, {{cog|da|græs|t=grass}}, {{cog|fo,is,nn|gras|t=grass}}, {{cog|nb|gras}}, {{m|nb|gress|t=grass}}, {{cog|sv|gräs|t=grass}}, {{cog|got|𐌲𐍂𐌰𐍃|t=herb}}; also {{cog|la|herba|t=plant, weed, grass}}, {{cog|sq|grath|t=grass blade, spike}}. Related to {{m|en|grow}}, {{m|en|green}}.
{{col-bottom}}

The "informer" sense is probably a shortening of {{m|en|grasshopper||police officer, informant}}, rhyming slang for {{m|en|copper||police officer}} or {{m|en|shopper||informant}}; the exact sequence of derivation is unclear.

