===Etymology 1===
[[File:Guard (2529280868).jpg|right|thumb|A guard (person protecting or watching over something)]]
{{etymon|en|id=noun|:inh|enm:garde|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|garde}}, from early {{der|en|frm|-}} or late {{der|en|fro|guarde|t=a guardian, warden, keeper}} (whence modern {{cog|fr|garde}}), from the verb {{m|fro|guarder}}. {{doublet|en|garda}}, which is from {{cog|ga|-}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

